    "author": "pablobm",
    "created_at": "2026-10-12T16:26:50Z",
    "body": "In principle there should be some sort of validation to avoid setting a past date. However this causes an issue as there's always going to be a difference between `Time.zone.now` when the form is rendered and when the form is submitted and processed. Perhaps the solution is to set it to now if it receives a past date.\r\n\r\nExpiries should be rounded to the closest minute, at least when rendering the form. Otherwise the form doesn't work because the default [`step`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/input/datetime-local#step) is one minute, but we are setting times with seconds (well, 59 out of 60 times).\r\n\r\nAdd a test for the case when both relative and absolute are sent. Shouldn't happen, but just in case. Decide who should win.",
    "review_state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED"
  },
